      "name": "JSP webshells being dropped on unpatched PTC Windchill instances",
      "description": "The US Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) added a vulnerability (CVE-2026-12569) in Windchill and FlexPLM, two product lifecycle management software platforms developed by PTC, to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog. Entries in the KEV catalog don\u2019t contain links to reports of exploitation, but PTC\u2019s advisory keeps getting updated with indicators of compromise and advice for defenders, confirming that attackers are dropping JSP webshells on vulnerable systems.",
